@api = http://localhost:5093/api

### A1. Registrar empresa + primer Admin (201) — HU-01
# @name registro
POST {{api}}/enterprises/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enterpriseName": "Taller El Rapido",
  "enterpriseTypeId": "0192f000-0000-7000-8000-000000000101",
  "planId": "0192f000-0000-7000-8000-000000000201",
  "adminFullName": "Alana Admin",
  "adminEmail": "admin@elrapido.com",
  "password": "Admin1234"
}

### A2. Registrar con el mismo correo (409)
POST {{api}}/enterprises/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enterpriseName": "Otro taller",
  "enterpriseTypeId": "0192f000-0000-7000-8000-000000000101",
  "planId": "0192f000-0000-7000-8000-000000000201",
  "adminFullName": "Otra persona",
  "adminEmail": "admin@elrapido.com",
  "password": "Admin1234"
}

### A3. Registrar con contraseña débil (400)
POST {{api}}/enterprises/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enterpriseName": "Taller X",
  "enterpriseTypeId": "0192f000-0000-7000-8000-000000000101",
  "planId": "0192f000-0000-7000-8000-000000000201",
  "adminFullName": "X",
  "adminEmail": "x@x.com",
  "password": "123"
}

### A4. Login correcto (200) — HU-02. Las peticiones de clientes usan este token.
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@elrapido.com",
  "password": "Admin1234"
}

### A5. Login con contraseña incorrecta (401)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@elrapido.com",
  "password": "Incorrecta1"
}

### A6. Clientes SIN token (401)
GET {{api}}/customers

### 1. Listar clientes (200)
GET {{api}}/customers?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Accept: application/json

### 2. Crear cliente (201)
POST {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "María López",
  "phone": "9999-0000",
  "email": "maria@correo.com"
}

### 3. Crear cliente sin nombre (400)
POST {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "",
  "phone": "9999-0000"
}

### 4. Buscar por nombre o teléfono (200)
GET {{api}}/customers?search=María
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Crear otro cliente y guardar su id (201)
# @name crear
POST {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Carlos Mejía",
  "phone": "8888-1111",
  "email": "carlos@correo.com"
}

### 6. Consultar por Id (200)
GET {{api}}/customers/{{crear.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 7. Consultar un Id que no existe (404)
GET {{api}}/customers/0192f000-0000-7000-8000-000000000999
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 8. Editar el cliente (204)
PUT {{api}}/customers/{{crear.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Carlos Mejía Rodríguez",
  "phone": "8888-2222",
  "email": "carlos@correo.com"
}

### 9. Editar con correo inválido (400)
PUT {{api}}/customers/{{crear.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Carlos",
  "phone": "8888-2222",
  "email": "esto-no-es-correo"
}